==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|mechanical|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/məˈkænɪkli/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mechanically.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyph|en|me|chan|i|cal|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# From a [[mechanical]] [[point of view]].
#: {{coi|en|'''mechanically''' speaking}}
# In a mechanical manner, [[mindlessly]], [[thoughtlessly]], [[automatically]], without [[thinking]].
#* {{RQ:Cleland Fanny Hill|passage=My fears, however, made me '''mechanically''' close my thighs; but the very touch of his hand insinuated between them, disclosed them and opened a way for the main attack.}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|pages=183–184|volume=II|passage="Of what avail," and her eyes wandered '''mechanically''' round, "is all the luxury by which I am surrounded, if it serve only as a barrier to all kindly feelings?"}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Aziz Huq|journal=Politico|title=Conservatives on the Supreme Court May Not Fully Align With Trump|titleurl=https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2025/02/26/supreme-court-conservative-trump-agenda-00206066|date=February 26 2025|passage=Provided they stick to their legal priors, rather than voting '''mechanically''' as Republican appointees, the justices seem likely to split on some of these cases — with real consequences for Trump’s agenda.}}

